    <p>Regression testing is where most QA debt accumulates. Teams add features faster than they add regression tests. The suite grows stale. Coverage erodes. And then one release, something that worked perfectly for two years breaks silently because nobody was testing it anymore.</p>
    <p>A checklist-based approach to regression works when the list is honest about what actually needs testing rather than optimized for completion speed. This is that list.</p>

